managing regional administration

coordinating infrastructure

supervising regional institutions

reporting regional conditions to the Crown

coordinating disaster response

supporting public safety

promoting regional economic development

protecting regional heritage

implementing national preparedness programmes


Landeshüter are not independent rulers.

Their authority derives from the Crown and Constitution.

The Krönherr may dismiss a Landeshüter for:

incompetence

corruption

constitutional violations

serious misconduct

failure to perform duties

abuse of authority



