---

XIII. THE VOLKSENTSCHEID

The Volksentscheid shall be the principal instrument of direct democracy.

Citizens shall be eligible to participate in national Volksentscheide from the age of fourteen.

Volksentscheide may concern:

major legislation

constitutional amendments

major national projects

national policies

territorial questions

major governmental restructuring

other constitutionally permitted questions


The Krönherr may call a Volksentscheid whenever he considers public participation desirable.

The people may also demand a Volksentscheid through a constitutional citizen petition.

A national petition reaching the constitutionally defined threshold shall require the government to consider or hold the requested vote.

Major constitutional questions shall require higher thresholds than ordinary legislation.


---

XIV. REFERENDUM CATEGORIES

Volksentscheide shall generally be divided into two categories.

Binding Volksentscheid

The result is legally binding.

Advisory Volksentscheid

The result formally expresses the public will but does not automatically create law.

The referendum question must clearly state which type of vote is being conducted.

The Constitution shall identify subjects requiring mandatory binding referendums.

These may include:

fundamental constitutional restructuring

permanent territorial changes

abolition of the monarchy

major sovereignty changes

other exceptionally important constitutional questions



