establish independent defence relationships


All foreign policy shall ultimately prioritize:

Austrian sovereignty

Austrian security

Austrian economic interests

Austrian citizens

long-term national stability


Austria shall cooperate with Europe while retaining its ability to pursue an independent national policy.


---

L. CURRENCY AND ECONOMIC SOVEREIGNTY

The Austro-Crown Monarchy may maintain the euro or establish a separate Austrian currency depending upon future constitutional and economic decisions.

A separate currency shall only be established if the government determines that Austria possesses the economic institutions necessary to maintain monetary stability.

Currency reform shall not be pursued merely for symbolism.

Economic sovereignty must be balanced with financial stability.


---

LI. NATIONAL UNITY

Austro-Crownism recognizes the importance of regional identity.

A citizen may be:

Viennese

Lower Austrian

Upper Austrian

Styrian

Carinthian

Salzburgian

Tyrolean

Vorarlbergian

Burgenlandian


while simultaneously being Austrian.

Regional pride and national patriotism are not contradictions.

The Crown represents Austria as a whole.


---

LII. EMERGENCY POWERS

A national emergency may be declared when Austria faces:

war

armed attack

terrorism

catastrophic natural disaster

major infrastructure collapse

severe national security threats


A normal emergency declaration shall last a limited period, such as thirty days.

Extensions shall require constitutional justification and consultation with the Krönrat.

Emergency powers may temporarily restrict certain activities necessary to protect the population.

They shall not be used to permanently abolish constitutional rights.

The government shall publish the justification for extraordinary emergency measures wherever national security permits.


---

LIII. CORRUPTION

Corruption shall be treated as a serious crime.

Senior officials shall be subject to:

financial disclosure requirements

independent auditing

anti-corruption investigations

criminal prosecution

removal from office

confiscation of illegally obtained assets where legally justified


The Crown's official finances shall be subject to appropriate auditing and transparency.

No official shall possess immunity for ordinary criminal conduct merely because of rank.


---

LIV. THE ECONOMIC AND SOCIAL ROLE OF THE CROWN

The Crown shall seek to create a society where:

citizens can work

families can prosper

healthcare is accessible

education is strong

infrastructure functions

businesses can grow

technology advances

Austria remains secure


The Crown shall not attempt to control every aspect of private life.

The state shall intervene primarily where intervention protects:

national sovereignty

public safety

economic stability

children

families

strategic industries

essential infrastructure

constitutional order



---

LV. THE FIVE GREAT PILLARS

Austro-Crownism ultimately rests upon five principal pillars.

THE CROWN

Strong hereditary national leadership, constitutional authority, stability, and continuity.

THE PEOPLE

Direct participation through Volksentscheide, petitions, demonstrations, consultations, and civic institutions.

AUSTRIA

A strong national identity based upon Austrian history, geography, culture, citizenship, sovereignty, and shared homeland.

DEFENCE

A highly prepared, modern, technologically advanced Austria capable of defending itself.

PROSPERITY

A capitalist economy strengthened through strategic state investment, technological development, infrastructure, employment, healthcare, and family support.


