LVII. FINAL DECLARATION

The Austro-Crown Monarchy shall not seek to become merely another European government.

It shall seek to become a distinct Austrian system combining hereditary Crown leadership with direct popular participation, strong national identity with civic equality, capitalism with social guarantees, military preparedness with civilian life, Catholic heritage with religious freedom, historical continuity with technological modernity, and powerful government with constitutional order.

The Crown shall provide continuity.

The People shall provide participation.

The Constitution shall provide order.

The armed forces shall provide defence.

The economy shall provide prosperity.

The family shall provide demographic continuity.

Education shall preserve the nation's memory.

